/target
# Cargo.lock is committed: reproducible, locked dependency resolution for
# the build/test/clippy gates (cargo … --locked). Do not re-ignore.
*.img
# ...except this one fixture, which IS committed. A mkfs.erofs built
# without libzstd cannot produce a zstd image, and most packaged builds
# are not built with it, so `tests/zstd_image.rs` carries the image
# rather than depending on what happens to be installed. Named
# individually rather than un-ignoring the whole directory, so a stray
# local image dropped in test-disks/ still stays out.
!test-disks/erofs-zstd-4k.img
*audit*
.history

# GSI test fixture (downloaded by tests/fixtures/download-gsi.sh).
# AOSP-licensed; not redistributed by this repo. The *.img rule above
# already covers system.img, but be explicit for the .tar / .zip
# intermediate forms as well.
tests/fixtures/*.img
tests/fixtures/*.tar*
tests/fixtures/*.zip

# chore fingerprint cache (sources:/generates: checksums). Derived data.
.chore/

# THE SUITE'S SCRATCH DIRECTORY, AND IT IS INSIDE THE REPOSITORY ON
# PURPOSE. The oracle tools run in the fs-linux-test-harness VM, which
# sees this repository at the path the host knows it by and nothing else
# of the host -- so an image under /tmp is a path the tool asked to read
# it cannot open. scripts/test.sh and fs_erofs_test_support::temp_dir
# both put scratch here, and the tier logs live in tmp/logs/.
/tmp/

# The harness's shared directory (fs-linux-test-harness.toml's [share]):
# what a run hands across to the guest and back.
/.vm-share/

# Build output. `chore staticlib` writes the archive and headers here for a
# consumer to copy out of (`chore artifact` prints this directory).
/dist/
.DS_Store

# THE FUZZ CORPUS IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, and `*.img` above would
# otherwise swallow it silently. The images under fuzz/corpus/ are not
# build output or fixtures a script regenerates on demand -- they are
# the seeds the gate in tests/fuzz_decoders.rs replays and mutates, and
# without them that suite has nothing to run and says so only once CI
# has already gone red.
!fuzz/corpus/**
